{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed shutter&#39;s siting and appearance would be out of the local character and result in an abrupt impact on the street scene by protruding the current building line of the terrace row. It would also set an inadequate precedent for the surrounding shops to propose the similar development. As such, the proposed development is considered unacceptable and contrary to: - National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, 2023); - Policies D4 &amp; D8 of the London Plan (March 2021); - Policy CP3 of the LBBD&#39;s Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010); - Policy BP11 of the LBBD&#39;s Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011); and - Policies SP2, SP4 &amp; DMD1 of the LBBD’s Draft Local Plan (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)."
  ],
